  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "TANH divides SINH(x) by an expm1-based denominator for |x| < 1 (and COSH(x) for |x| >= 1) in x87, saturating to +/-1",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20326 through 20527, TANH(number) computes RN53(RN64(SINH(x) / denominator)), where denominator is (RN53(RN64(expm1(x) + expm1(-x))) + 2) / 2 in x87 for |x| < 1 (distinct from public COSH) and COSH(x) for |x| >= 1, saturating to +/-1.0 on large |x| via SATURATE_SIGN. Of 39,028 full-bank TANH rows, 39,025 match and 3 differ by 1 ULP.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20430 (39,025/39,028 full-bank and 120/120 pinned TANH rows) and 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 229).",
